{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateFSTrichotomy"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.fsType_not_determined_by_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.fsType_not_determined_by_dual","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.lean#L133-L147","doc":"**The ambient involution does not decide the gate.**  Over one fixed\nduality datum there are three-dimensional candidates on both sides: one passes\nthe `Sym²` gate, one fails it.\n\nSo an argument of the form *\"the ambient group has a non-trivial outer\nautomorphism, therefore the three-dimensional object it carries is\nnon-self-dual\"* has no force — the conclusion is independent of the premise.\nFrobenius–Schur type is a property of the representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.real_candidate_fails","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.real_candidate_fails","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.lean#L128-L129","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.complex_candidate_passes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.complex_candidate_passes","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.lean#L124-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.candidate_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.candidate_dim","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.lean#L122-L122","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.fsReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.fsReal","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.lean#L118-L120","doc":"The candidate read as **real** type — same index set, same multiplicities,\nsame dimensions, same duality involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.fsComplex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.fsComplex","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.lean#L115-L116","doc":"The candidate read as **complex** type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.dThree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.dThree","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.lean#L112-L113","doc":"Three-dimensional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.mOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.mOne","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.lean#L109-L110","doc":"One irrep, occurring once. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.dualInv_no_fixed_point","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.dualInv_no_fixed_point","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.lean#L104-L105","doc":"Non-trivial: it has no fixed point on `{0, 1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.dualInv_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.dualInv_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.dualInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.dualInv","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.lean#L99-L100","doc":"The duality involution: `0 ↔ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.selfDual_candidate_not_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.selfDual_candidate_not_three","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AmbientInvolutionDoesNotDecideType.lean#L75-L89","doc":"**The screen.**  A candidate all of whose occurring irreps are self-dual\ncannot be three-dimensional and pass the `Sym²` gate — no matter what duality\ninvolution the ambient group carries.\n\nThe ambient group appears nowhere in the hypotheses: the only inputs are the\nFrobenius–Schur types of the irreps actually occurring in the object. ","signatureChunk":0}]}